# Investigation Template

Use for an investigation that needs durable evidence. An unfilled template does not establish reproduction or a cause.

## Report and scope

Record expected behavior, observed failure, affected version/revision/environment, authorized scope, and sources. Separate the original report from your observations.

## Reproduction and observations

Record the actual inputs, preconditions, actions, and observed result, or explicitly state that reproduction is unavailable. Include source/cwd and relevant environment for executed commands. Protect sensitive inputs through safe references.

## Competing explanations

| Hypothesis | Supporting/contradicting evidence | Discriminating check | Actual outcome/status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |

Do not treat correlation as causation or invent a completed check.

## Conclusion and correction

State the supported cause and confidence, or the unresolved evidence gap. Record a correction only if implemented within authorization; include affected invariants and actual verification. Separate existing failures from new regressions where evidence permits.

## Next action

Name the concrete missing observation, unresolved risk, or follow-up. Stop when evidence is sufficient or a specific access/input gap prevents progress.
